Feature: nuka report --format allure writes a run as the TypeScript engine does

  nuka report --format allure writes one run as Allure results: one result per execution, with one step per line of the scenario, categories.json, and environment.properties.
  A result's history id is allure-js-commons' formula over its full name and its parameters, so a result keeps the history either engine's results built up.
  A claim is a child step of its Then, and a broken claim's step carries the failure marker its category matches.
  A line no step matches is broken, and the steps after it are skipped.

  Scenario: a judged claim, a broken claim, and the verdict of each criterion
    Given the project "judgments"
    When nuka runs "run"
    And nuka runs "report --format allure --out allure"
    Then it exits with 0
    And the allure results in "allure" are
